## UNCONTROLLABLE URGE (instrumental cover) for PULP/SKRED
#  184 BPM, key of A, 136 bars (about 2:57). Instrumental only, no vocals or lyrics.
#  Self-contained: drums are built-in waves 82-99.
#     [devo_uncontrollable_urge.sk] /ls      then:   play     (stop:  stop)
#
#  WHAT THE SOURCES SAID
#    - key A and a tempo around 184 (variable in the record, one site lists 91,
#      which is half time). Constant 184 here.
#    - bass: a steady eighth-note tonic drone, with a 3-note pickup riff in the
#      intro (tonic on beat 1, then 3 notes a whole tone below on the last
#      three eighths of the bar)
#    - chorus: power chords, V - IV - I (E5, D5, A in this key)
#    - lots of start-stop breaks
#  GUESSES (not verified, edit freely)
#    - the arrangement and section lengths (the record has long drone vamps)
#    - the drum feel (kick on 1 and 3, snare on 2 and 4, eighth-note hats)
#    - the guitar chug rhythm, the synth stab accents, and every mix level
#  UNTESTED and UNHEARD at the time of writing.
#
#  VOICE MAP
#    v0 kick  v1 snare  v2 closed hat  v3 open hat  v5 crash
#    v6 bass saw (centre) + v7 detuned square partner (right)
#    v8 guitar power chord: root, v9 fifth (+7), v10 octave (+12)
#    v11 FM metal stab + v12 its modulator
#  PATTERNS  0 conductor  1 kick  2 snare  3 hats  4 intro bass riff
#            5 verse bass drone  8 chorus bass  9 chorus guitar
#            10 verse guitar chug  11 stab  13 snare roll
#  SECTIONS (bar numbers)
#     0-7 intro   8-15 start-stop   16-31 verse   32-47 chorus
#     48-55 start-stop   56-71 verse   72-87 chorus   88-95 start-stop
#     96-111 final chorus   112-135 outro vamp   136 hard stop and cleanup
# ======================================================================

[UNCONTROLLABLE URGE] puts
M 184 16

## DELAY BUS (stab echo only, the record is mostly dry)
DS 1 184 .75
DL 1 - - 6 2 2 9
DD 1 7 3

## VOICES
v0 w82 f440 a6 p0                                # kick
v1 w83 f440 a7 p0                                # snare
v2 w84 f440 a-3 p.25                             # closed hat
v3 w85 f440 a-2 p-.25                            # open hat
v5 w94 f440 a4 p.2                               # crash

# bass: plucky saw plus detuned square partner on the right
v6 w15 a-1 p0 t.002,.14,.25,.06 j1 k1300 q1.8
v6 >7
v7 w16 a-6 N0,8 p.4
v6 G7 H7

# guitar power chord from ONE note: v8 root, v9 fifth, v10 octave, bright and spread
v8 w15 a-8 p-.25 t.002,.09,.15,.05 j1 k3800 q.7 c4,.15
v8 >9
v8 >10
v9 N7 a-10 p.3
v10 N12 a-12 p-.5
v8 G9,10 H9,10

# metal FM stab (copied from hammer_the_signal.sk), modulator tracks pitch
v11 w0 a-2 p-.35 t.001,.45,0,.35 FF2 FB4 F12,2.2 G12 H12
v12 w0 a0 t.001,.30,0,.30 N21 m1

## EVENTS (end-of-song cleanup responder)
[O DQ] /ceb 4 99
/cer 1

